# WP Admin Reskin Guidelines

This rules file provides context for the WordPress 7.0 admin visual reskin project.

## Project Scope

This is a **CSS-only visual refresh** of the WordPress admin. No markup changes, no JavaScript changes, no new functionality.

### What we are doing
- Updating button, input, notice, card, and table styles
- Aligning with the WordPress Design System
- Using existing CSS custom properties from `wp-base-styles`
- Using Sass for any additional tokenization

### What we are NOT doing
- Changing HTML markup
- Adding new CSS custom properties (backward compat concern)
- Adopting DataViews functionality
- Restructuring admin layout or navigation

## Available CSS Custom Properties

The `wp-base-styles` stylesheet is loaded on all admin screens and provides these variables per color scheme:

```css
/* Theme color (accent) */
--wp-admin-theme-color: #3858e9;           /* Modern scheme example */
--wp-admin-theme-color--rgb: 56, 88, 233;  /* For rgba() usage */
--wp-admin-theme-color-darker-10: #2145e6; /* Hover state */
--wp-admin-theme-color-darker-20: #183ad6; /* Active state */

/* Focus ring */
--wp-admin-border-width-focus: 2px;        /* 1.5px on retina */
```

### Usage examples

```css
/* Primary button background */
.button-primary {
  background-color: var(--wp-admin-theme-color);
}

/* Hover state */
.button-primary:hover {
  background-color: var(--wp-admin-theme-color-darker-10);
}

/* Focus ring */
.button:focus {
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 var(--wp-admin-border-width-focus) var(--wp-admin-theme-color);
}

/* Semi-transparent using RGB variant */
.selected-row {
  background-color: rgba(var(--wp-admin-theme-color--rgb), 0.04);
}
```

